1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,500
Rush hour. The elephant bus just picked up something that isn't a passenger.

2
00:00:02,700 --> 00:00:05,100
A few hours earlier. Mochi had missed the boat home.

3
00:00:05,300 --> 00:00:09,700
But there's a sign. Whales, that way.

4
00:00:09,900 --> 00:00:14,300
The problem: it's rush hour.

5
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:19,100
In this city, the bus is an elephant.

6
00:00:19,300 --> 00:00:21,700
A packed bus feels the same in every world.

7
00:00:21,900 --> 00:00:24,300
The whale sign is getting smaller. Wrong direction.

8
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:26,900
The stop cord hangs from the elephant's ear. A bit high.

9
00:00:27,100 --> 00:00:31,500
Thank you, Mr. Giraffe.

10
00:00:31,700 --> 00:00:33,900
The traffic light is a chameleon. Green means go.

11
00:00:34,100 --> 00:00:38,900
Unless a strawberry truck drives by.

12
00:00:39,100 --> 00:00:43,900
The subway is dug by a mole. In real time.

13
00:00:44,100 --> 00:00:46,500
For a penguin, a packed subway is a little warm.

14
00:00:46,700 --> 00:00:51,300
Forget the whale for now. Somewhere cold first.

15
00:00:51,500 --> 00:00:56,300
The smell of cold air. The nose moves first. Again.

16
00:00:56,500 --> 00:00:58,900
Found it. A tiny Antarctica.

17
00:00:59,100 --> 00:01:01,300
It was delivery time.

18
00:01:01,500 --> 00:01:06,500
The truck heads away from the whales.

19
00:01:06,700 --> 00:01:10,500
And Mochi was not alone. (To be continued)

